---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";

export const prerender = true;
---

<Layout
  title="How the math works | Fuel Calculate"
  description="The exact formulas Fuel Calculate uses for trip cost, fuel comparison, and monthly/yearly projections."
>
  <Hero eyebrow="Transparent by default" title="How the math works." />

  <section class="mx-auto flex max-w-[720px] flex-col gap-2xl px-md pb-5xl sm:px-lg">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Cost per km</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        For petrol, diesel, E20, CNG and LPG, cost per km is just price divided by
        mileage:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-sm overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-ink p-md text-code text-on-primary">costPerKm = pricePerUnit / mileage</pre>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        For EV, mileage is expressed as efficiency (kWh per 100km) rather than
        km-per-unit, since that's the standard way EV efficiency is measured — this
        avoids an inverted-unit mistake:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-sm overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-ink p-md text-code text-on-primary">costPerKm = (tariffPerKwh * efficiencyKwhPer100Km) / 100</pre>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Trip cost</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        Round trip doubles the one-way distance before the cost is applied:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-sm overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-ink p-md text-code text-on-primary">effectiveDistance = roundTrip ? distanceOneWay * 2 : distanceOneWay
tripCost = costPerKm * effectiveDistance</pre>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Comparing fuels</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        Every fuel you select is costed for the same trip distance. One fuel is the
        baseline (defaults to Petrol); every other fuel shows its ₹ and % difference
        against it — negative means cheaper:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-sm overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-ink p-md text-code text-on-primary">deltaVsBaseline = cost[fuel] - cost[baseline]
percentDiff = (deltaVsBaseline / cost[baseline]) * 100</pre>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Monthly &amp; yearly projection</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        Built from your daily commute pattern, not a guess at "working days" — you set
        days-per-month explicitly:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-sm overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-ink p-md text-code text-on-primary">dailyDistance = distancePerTrip * tripsPerDay * (roundTrip ? 2 : 1)
dailyCost = costPerKm * dailyDistance
monthlyCost = dailyCost * daysPerMonth
yearlyCost = monthlyCost * 12</pre>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        Yearly is derived from the monthly figure (×12), not a separate ×365 daily
        calculation — so the two numbers never quietly disagree with each other.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
